# Build context exclusions for the builds whose context is this directory
# (hypervisor.Containerfile and the nvidia/amd variants). build-minimal uses
# manifests/ as its context and is unaffected.
#
# This is not a size optimisation with a correctness side effect — it is the
# other way round. `.gitignore` does not exclude anything from a podman build
# context, so every local build artifact under this tree got tarred up and
# handed to the builder. workloadctl/rpmbuild/ is the one that bites: the
# rpm-builder stage COPYs workloadctl/ wholesale, so a host that has ever run
# `just rpm-build` shipped its whole RPM history into the stage, and the
# `workloadctl-*.rpm` glob downstream then matched every one of them.
#
# Anything COPYed by a Containerfile must stay out of this list even when it is
# gitignored — bin/cosy, man/cosy.1 and the generated policy.json all are.

.git
.gitignore

# Upstream source clones kept for reference (gigabytes, never built from).
.reference

# Local build output.
workloadctl/rpmbuild
rpm/rpm-output
output
base-images
bootc-src
manifests
rpmmd
store

# Editor / agent / test tooling state.
.idea
.claude
.mcp.json
__pycache__
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
